WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:03.850
- The number one reason I push patience

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:06.893
is 'cause patience will give
you the air cover to take risk.

00:00:09.706 --> 00:00:11.871
If you realize how,

00:00:11.871 --> 00:00:13.540
do you know what I wish

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:15.780
for all of you 25 year olds in here?

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:18.163
That you knew how long you'd feel at 40.

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:21.910
'Cause 40's fucking old to you,

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:23.600
I was just there

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:28.263
and news alert, you're gonna
kind of feel exactly the same.

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:30.771
And when you understand that,

00:00:30.771 --> 00:00:33.600
and then once you go insular,

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.950
one of the reasons maybe
I've never had a mentor

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:37.277
is 'cause I don't value
anybody else's opinion

00:00:37.277 --> 00:00:38.993
more than my own.

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:42.549
And it's a very,

00:00:42.549 --> 00:00:46.127
and I'll tell you why that's important,

00:00:46.127 --> 00:00:48.830
because if I lose, then I deserve it.

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:51.204
Because then if I win, I deserve it.

00:00:51.204 --> 00:00:54.870
But the way to really eliminate fear

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:57.660
is by not giving a fuck
about anybody's opinion.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:59.570
My losses are mine.

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:01.470
I'll deal with them myself.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:02.840
I don't need your two cents,

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:04.693
you're losing plenty on your own.

00:01:05.976 --> 00:01:10.976
That, patience and inner voice,

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:13.013
makes you unbeatable.

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:15.943
It's crazy how I feel my whole life,

00:01:15.943 --> 00:01:17.540
never had peer pressure,

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:20.420
never did anything, anything, ever, ever

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:21.930
that I didn't want to do

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:22.940
because I just didn't value

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:25.440
somebody else's opinion over mine.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:28.740
And that comes from good
parenting, circumstance, DNA,

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:30.300
a million fucking things.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:31.951
I don't know how to teach that.

00:01:31.951 --> 00:01:33.290
What I'm just trying to do

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:34.820
is I'm trying to become,

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:36.705
in a weird way I like being popular

00:01:36.705 --> 00:01:39.253
because I become your courage.

00:01:40.348 --> 00:01:42.080
I think the most flattering thing

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:43.323
that's happening to me in my life

00:01:43.323 --> 00:01:45.533
is I'm becoming people's courage

00:01:45.533 --> 00:01:48.712
because when they take risk
and they take ridicule,

00:01:48.712 --> 00:01:50.423
they point to me.

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:54.113
And I tell their parents
to go fuck themselves.

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:57.300
And that's a very, very, very interesting,

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.070
if you look, I don't know how deep

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:00.130
any of you are in my content,

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:02.640
I know you are John,
that is what I'm doing,

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:03.630
that is what I'm doing,

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:04.770
and it's a very good feeling,

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:05.603
I feel very happy

00:02:05.603 --> 00:02:07.610
'cause I think I'm bringing people value

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:11.010
because let me tell you what's
way more scary than failure,

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:12.550
regret,

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:13.900
you just don't know it yet.

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:20.260
Regret is fucking poison

00:02:21.212 --> 00:02:22.590
and you start feeling it

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:25.002
when you can't do anything about it.

00:02:25.002 --> 00:02:27.240
And I have a funny feeling when you're 65,

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:28.730
you don't feel that
much different than 40,

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:30.820
you don't feel that
much different than 25.

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:33.320
The problem is you're
starting to run out of time.

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:36.270
Got it?

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:37.422
But I agree with you,

00:02:37.422 --> 00:02:39.604
the relationship with parenting

00:02:39.604 --> 00:02:42.820
and the conservative nature of the culture

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:44.490
leads to a lot of that

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:45.960
which is too bad

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:48.030
because you think you're
doing your parents a favor

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:49.270
by appeasing them

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:52.142
but later in life you're
gonna really be mad at them

00:02:52.142 --> 00:02:53.996
and resent them

00:02:53.996 --> 00:02:56.073
and it's not gonna play out.

00:02:57.344 --> 00:02:59.927
(gentle music)

